{
  "_comment": "Form ids and logical field -> question mapping. Each field: {id, title}. A set id (the Tally question uuid) is matched first; otherwise the exact title (whitespace-normalised). The ids are the form-builder uuids. The REST API gives each question a short id, so an id is matched against the question id and against its fields' uuid / blockGroupUuid. Hidden fields (recipe, dish, version) are fields of the one HIDDEN_FIELDS question: their id is the field uuid, matched before the field name. Run `python3 build.py discover` to list questions and `python3 build.py shapes` to see answer structure. Only the allow-listed recipe text fields may be mapped: any other field name, a consent entry included, stops the build, and a consent question left on a form is ignored. Choice answers are never matched by guessing: contribution/overall use the configured option texts (an option uuid in an answer is first turned into its text); finished uses option positions.",
  "target_tests": 5,
